WEBVTT

03:57.529 --> 03:59.156
The battle...

04:00.699 --> 04:01.825
It is won.

04:25.265 --> 04:26.516
I...

04:53.376 --> 04:54.669
What have you done?

04:59.966 --> 05:01.176
Jace.

05:09.935 --> 05:11.061
Jace.

05:13.563 --> 05:14.898
What have you done?

05:41.091 --> 05:42.425
How could you?

05:48.557 --> 05:51.685
How could you do this? How?

05:54.729 --> 05:57.399
How could you do this to me?

05:58.400 --> 05:59.734
You answer me!

06:05.448 --> 06:07.367
How could you do this?

06:08.785 --> 06:12.622
You answer me! Please!

06:14.124 --> 06:16.626
How could you do this?

06:16.710 --> 06:19.212
Your Grace, leave him.

06:19.296 --> 06:21.047
You must leave him, Your Grace.

06:22.424 --> 06:25.176
How dare you set your hands on me!

06:25.260 --> 06:26.678
How dare you!

06:46.865 --> 06:48.033
My queen...

06:50.784 --> 06:52.120
I have failed you.

06:59.711 --> 07:01.254
My life must be forfeit.

07:03.924 --> 07:05.592
And what good would that do?

07:07.427 --> 07:09.179
Will it wake my son?

07:10.931 --> 07:15.352
Will it change the truth
of his folly and yours?

07:18.229 --> 07:19.230
And yours!

07:20.190 --> 07:23.902
All of you who knew what
Jacaerys had done and stood by.

07:24.861 --> 07:26.321
Are your lives, too, not forfeit?

07:26.404 --> 07:29.407
Have you not betrayed your queen?

08:18.164 --> 08:19.832
Lord Corlys!

08:35.724 --> 08:37.225
Lord Corlys!

08:43.523 --> 08:45.150
Lord Corlys!

08:55.618 --> 08:57.078
Whoa, calm.

09:16.347 --> 09:17.348
Help me.

09:18.391 --> 09:19.350
My lady.

09:20.518 --> 09:22.771
I have done a terrible thing.

09:24.230 --> 09:25.982
Why have you come here?

09:27.650 --> 09:28.735
There was a battle.

09:28.818 --> 09:30.820
The prince Jacaerys, it seems, is dead.

09:36.576 --> 09:39.746
-You need to go now.
-Oh, there was ships and smoke.

09:39.829 --> 09:41.790
I wanted only to help, truly.

09:41.873 --> 09:43.917
-But Sheepstealer was frightened, so--
-I don't care.

09:45.877 --> 09:47.754
You were supposed to be
on a ship to Pentos.

09:47.837 --> 09:50.090
Well, I need asylum, my lady.

09:50.173 --> 09:53.093
-I had nowhere else to go.
-How dare you? Asylum?

09:53.176 --> 09:56.429
You run from my charge
and you bring disaster to my doorstep.

09:56.513 --> 09:59.182
-The queen will be hunting you.
-None saw that it was me.

10:01.351 --> 10:03.061
I would say you had lost all sense,

10:03.144 --> 10:05.063
but then I doubt you had
any in the first place.

10:07.941 --> 10:09.275
Don't come back here.

10:12.654 --> 10:14.197
Do you want a dragon or not?

10:16.116 --> 10:18.993
You said yourself you were deceived
in your dealings with the queen.

10:20.078 --> 10:21.454
Taken for a fool.

10:23.039 --> 10:25.500
You wanted protection. I offer it now.

10:32.423 --> 10:33.842
Vhagar is at large.

10:35.218 --> 10:37.720
Sheepstealer has long made his home here.

10:37.804 --> 10:39.222
All we need from you...

10:40.557 --> 10:41.850
is blindness.

10:49.440 --> 10:50.942
The Vale is vast.

10:52.610 --> 10:55.321
I cannot stop a dragon
from abiding where it pleases.

10:57.782 --> 11:00.451
I do not wish to see you again.

11:06.541 --> 11:08.710
I tell a tale of a fearsome war

11:08.793 --> 11:10.170
Thank our lucky stones

11:10.253 --> 11:12.463
10,000 came, but we had more

11:12.547 --> 11:14.340
And pressed 'em to the bloody shore

11:14.424 --> 11:16.176
Now we can't see the water's floor

11:16.259 --> 11:17.677
Hey, hey, hey!

11:17.760 --> 11:19.304
'Cause the lake's full of their bones

11:21.014 --> 11:22.307
-Fish feed!
-Fish feed!

11:22.390 --> 11:24.559
-Fish feed!
-Fish feed!

11:24.642 --> 11:26.311
Smashed to smithereens!

11:26.394 --> 11:28.021
Fish feed! Fish feed!

11:28.104 --> 11:29.814
Fish feed!

11:29.898 --> 11:31.608
We drowned the fucking Greens

11:31.691 --> 11:33.735
I tell you a tale of a cunning trick

11:33.818 --> 11:35.195
How did it come to pass?

11:35.278 --> 11:37.071
Aemond comes, they said, run quick!

11:37.155 --> 11:39.157
With his one good eye,
he looks a prick

11:39.240 --> 11:41.784
And we've got Daemon, so go stick...

11:42.410 --> 11:44.954
...your dragon up your ass!

11:45.997 --> 11:47.999
Ser Simon Strong, Your Grace.

11:48.082 --> 11:50.168
Well, well, well.

11:51.211 --> 11:52.921
Reminds you of the old times.

11:54.255 --> 11:55.715
When the Riverlands were ascendant,

11:55.798 --> 11:58.468
music and meat and virile young men.

11:59.761 --> 12:03.431
And which of these delights drew you to us
through glade and glen?

12:03.514 --> 12:08.645
I bring gifts, in token of your victories
at the Red Fork and on the lakeshore.

12:09.729 --> 12:12.607
The finest wine
from House Strong's cellars.

12:12.690 --> 12:14.317
Whoa!

12:15.276 --> 12:16.444
Wine!

12:17.654 --> 12:19.239
And a message for you.

12:22.617 --> 12:23.743
From the queen.

12:43.930 --> 12:45.014
Your Grace?

12:45.765 --> 12:47.141
Is there something amiss?

12:51.938 --> 12:53.690
The crown prince is dead.

12:56.526 --> 12:59.862
I'm summoned now to King's Landing
to claim the Iron Throne for our queen.

12:59.946 --> 13:02.573
I charge you to march south
and meet me there.

13:02.657 --> 13:05.368
And send men to garrison Harrenhal,
but march with strength.

13:05.451 --> 13:07.704
And when Rhaenyra
has claimed the Iron Throne,

13:07.787 --> 13:09.872
we will send dragons
to scour the skies above you.

13:09.956 --> 13:11.874
Be cunning, be steadfast.

13:11.958 --> 13:13.918
Cut down any who remain to resist you.

13:15.461 --> 13:17.171
We will be the queen's fist.

13:17.255 --> 13:19.215
None will stand against us.

13:27.598 --> 13:28.808
To King's Landing!

13:30.601 --> 13:33.604
-And the day we meet again.
-King's Landing!

13:39.152 --> 13:42.363
I have seen that your coming
has been an omen of the end.

13:43.031 --> 13:45.992
-The end of what?
-Many things.

13:48.995 --> 13:50.580
And the beginning of others.

13:50.663 --> 13:52.623
I would thank you for your help,
but I'm not sure yet

13:52.707 --> 13:54.083
what your purpose has been.

13:54.167 --> 13:55.710
I've done the queen a service.

13:55.793 --> 13:58.379
I put 40,000 rivermen at her call.

13:59.714 --> 14:00.840
Tell her...

14:02.050 --> 14:03.217
I want Harrenhal.

14:05.720 --> 14:07.889
I've lived there all my long life,

14:07.972 --> 14:10.475
and I've seen it given from hand to hand.

14:10.558 --> 14:12.769
And yet none seem to cherish it.

14:12.852 --> 14:15.063
Why should it not come to me?

14:16.439 --> 14:20.902
You have neither name, nor title,
nor noble husband.

14:22.111 --> 14:26.157
The crown is not in the habit
of giving out castles to midwives.

14:27.658 --> 14:30.244
And is midwife the sum
of what you think I am?

14:35.458 --> 14:37.502
I will speak with her. Perhaps there is...

14:38.628 --> 14:40.797
some other reward she may extend your way.

14:41.506 --> 14:43.132
Some other reward?

14:45.051 --> 14:47.470
I ask for food and you offer me rubies.

14:49.680 --> 14:51.140
For all their worth...

14:52.767 --> 14:55.019
they will never satisfy my hunger.

14:57.855 --> 14:59.148
Go home, Daemon.

15:00.817 --> 15:02.693
But do not come back here.

15:04.153 --> 15:05.696
Remember what I told you.

15:51.033 --> 15:53.411
Many before have left
my grandsire for dead,

15:53.494 --> 15:55.580
and they were all mistaken.

15:56.581 --> 15:57.832
We will find him.

16:07.967 --> 16:08.968
Oh!

16:14.682 --> 16:15.892
You...

16:17.185 --> 16:18.853
You knew him as a child.

16:21.647 --> 16:23.900
He was stern...

16:25.776 --> 16:26.903
but gentle.

16:28.112 --> 16:29.197
At least in my eyes.

16:30.031 --> 16:31.574
He loved my grandmother

16:31.657 --> 16:34.452
more than few men
I have seen love their wives.

16:34.535 --> 16:36.204
It was for her sake...

16:37.121 --> 16:41.209
I think, that he tried
to forget about you.

16:43.586 --> 16:44.795
Your brother told me.

16:48.549 --> 16:51.427
We were not mere memories to be forgotten.

16:53.012 --> 16:54.013
No.

16:56.390 --> 16:58.142
He is proud as well,

16:58.226 --> 16:59.685
to his detriment.

17:00.603 --> 17:01.646
Stiff of neck.

17:05.858 --> 17:06.858
Ah.

17:08.069 --> 17:11.155
That side of him, I know.

17:12.865 --> 17:13.782
Knew.

17:15.159 --> 17:16.953
I will not say so yet.

17:24.252 --> 17:25.377
And your betrothed?

17:26.546 --> 17:27.964
We were children together.

17:31.175 --> 17:33.844
I'm tired of losing people, Alyn.

17:42.144 --> 17:43.771
He's searching, too.

18:46.417 --> 18:49.045
-You seem to be in less pain.
-No, I'm not.

18:50.796 --> 18:52.131
You no longer ask for milk of the poppy--

18:52.214 --> 18:53.924
That's because I'm not
fucking speaking to you.

18:54.008 --> 18:55.009
Right.

18:55.718 --> 18:57.261
You're still furious
that I saved your life.

18:57.345 --> 18:58.971
You betrayed my identity to our captors.

18:59.055 --> 19:01.057
Who you needlessly antagonized,
Your Grace.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.767
They were going to murder you.

19:03.893 --> 19:05.728
You are at least now

19:05.811 --> 19:07.688
headed in the right direction
towards the coast.

19:07.772 --> 19:09.357
Yeah, and what happens when we get there?

19:09.440 --> 19:10.816
When we're dragged before Rhaenyra

19:10.900 --> 19:13.778
and her gloating fucking court of cunts?

19:16.155 --> 19:17.323
What is it?

19:19.784 --> 19:20.785
What is it?

19:21.661 --> 19:22.787
I can see only the road behind us,

19:22.870 --> 19:24.872
but I shouldn't be surprised if there is--

19:29.794 --> 19:31.545
I was mistaken. I am surprised.

19:36.926 --> 19:38.594
That peacock Tyland Lannister

19:38.678 --> 19:41.889
has actually convinced the Triarchy
to come into it against Rhaenyra.

19:43.307 --> 19:44.725
Though it doesn't seem
to have gone very well.

19:45.851 --> 19:47.103
Get them back inside!

19:49.855 --> 19:51.941
You heard him! Inside!

19:58.656 --> 20:01.367
It seems our journey to Dragonstone
will be somewhat delayed.

20:19.093 --> 20:20.136
Your Grace.

20:21.303 --> 20:23.472
You should take shelter
in the forest, and quickly.

20:23.556 --> 20:25.433
I have gold enough to buy our berth.

20:25.516 --> 20:26.809
We can make our way to Duskendale.

20:26.892 --> 20:28.310
We are going to Rook's Rest.

20:29.562 --> 20:31.897
We would be wise to avoid that place.
We could be captured again.

20:31.981 --> 20:33.816
Cole has a garrison there, does he not?

20:33.899 --> 20:35.901
-They will be loyal to me.
-But the road there, Your Grace,

20:35.985 --> 20:37.319
is long and perilous.

20:43.993 --> 20:45.703
If this be victory...

20:46.829 --> 20:48.372
I hope I never see another.

21:05.848 --> 21:08.184
Alyn, I have nothing to give you now.

21:09.351 --> 21:10.770
But my name.

21:22.823 --> 21:26.452
And yet I count that of more worth...

21:27.828 --> 21:29.371
than a mountain of gold.

22:08.410 --> 22:10.454
I would speak with Commander Largent.

22:16.836 --> 22:18.420
Then speak, Your Grace.

22:21.882 --> 22:24.552
I regret intruding
on your Gold Cloaks, but...

22:26.679 --> 22:28.305
the matter is grave.

22:29.765 --> 22:32.560
If word were to seep out,
it would spell death for all involved.

22:38.941 --> 22:40.776
Rhaenyra is returning.

22:43.654 --> 22:45.155
How come you by this knowledge?

22:45.239 --> 22:46.657
In the prince regent's absence,

22:46.740 --> 22:49.076
Queen Helaena holds
the authority of the city.

22:50.119 --> 22:51.537
She intends, in the interest of peace,

22:51.620 --> 22:55.374
to allow Rhaenyra to enter the Red Keep,
and to then take the throne.

22:56.417 --> 22:58.460
-Some would call that treason.
-Some would.

23:00.754 --> 23:02.298
The question is, would you?

23:29.366 --> 23:30.993
The Rogue Prince himself.

23:36.874 --> 23:38.208
What are you doing here?

23:39.335 --> 23:40.753
My prince.

23:40.836 --> 23:42.713
We are just returned from Harrenhal.

23:42.796 --> 23:44.298
And the Gullet.

23:45.090 --> 23:47.927
We weren't sure if we should go up there.

23:49.637 --> 23:51.221
A terrible thing has happened.

23:53.223 --> 23:55.351
The queen wished you
to attack or pursue Vhagar.

23:57.770 --> 23:58.979
Or am I mistaken?

23:59.855 --> 24:02.191
Aemond did not come.

24:04.234 --> 24:07.655
And you waited two days only
before resigning your mission?

24:08.322 --> 24:09.156
Addam left, too.

24:09.239 --> 24:12.785
We thought there might be
some misunderstanding.

24:13.744 --> 24:16.038
I was unaware Her Grace,
the queen, had required of you

24:16.121 --> 24:20.000
in this moment, or any other,
your thoughts.

24:23.462 --> 24:25.798
There's something wrong
in those woods, though.

24:25.881 --> 24:26.966
I'm telling you.

24:27.967 --> 24:31.136
We heard all kinds of sounds,
like voices. I saw a--

24:36.141 --> 24:37.476
You have erred.

24:38.560 --> 24:40.521
All three of you,
and your error will cost us dearly.

24:40.604 --> 24:42.314
I left a garrison there, and a household.

24:42.398 --> 24:45.442
There was a woman
who brought news of a battle.

24:45.526 --> 24:46.819
A maester, I thought.

24:46.902 --> 24:47.903
Or...

24:48.529 --> 24:50.155
maybe a witch.

24:52.491 --> 24:54.368
-Where is your comrade?
-He's gone with the Lady Baela

24:54.451 --> 24:55.619
back to the Gullet.

25:00.916 --> 25:03.460
Should we return now
to Harrenhal, my prince?

25:18.559 --> 25:19.810
Is she inside?

25:20.811 --> 25:23.313
She has not wished to be seen since Jace.

25:24.898 --> 25:27.693
And meanwhile, the smith and the sot
allow Aemond One-Eye

25:27.776 --> 25:29.987
-to fly through their fingers.
-She is in grief.

25:30.070 --> 25:31.947
-Do you question her methods?
-Not hers.

25:32.948 --> 25:34.074
Theirs.

25:34.742 --> 25:35.826
And yours.

25:36.910 --> 25:38.412
I left you here a prisoner.

25:38.495 --> 25:41.290
Having forsaken the promise
that you made to me.

25:41.373 --> 25:44.126
You've wriggled your way
toward the crown like an eel.

25:44.209 --> 25:47.379
I confess, I underestimated
your slipperiness.

25:47.463 --> 25:50.174
Bait me all you wish.

25:50.257 --> 25:53.927
I have the queen's trust,
which you have yet to earn.

25:54.011 --> 25:56.263
-The queen is my wife.
-Then why have you added

25:56.346 --> 25:57.848
to what she must already suffer?

25:57.931 --> 25:59.767
What is between us
is none of your concern.

26:01.477 --> 26:02.811
What game are you playing?

26:03.896 --> 26:07.024
Retribution for insults, real or imagined?

26:08.734 --> 26:11.737
Do you coil yourself here
in order to strike at me?

26:13.572 --> 26:16.575
Not everything is about you, Daemon.

26:29.338 --> 26:31.840
Aemond is unaccounted for, then.

26:46.980 --> 26:49.858
Do you believe
the queen's judgment to be sound?

26:49.942 --> 26:51.902
I would not serve her otherwise.

26:53.153 --> 26:56.406
But she has staked much on
the word of Alicent Hightower.

26:56.490 --> 26:57.950
Hm, aye.

26:59.159 --> 27:00.619
I was not present at their meeting.

27:01.620 --> 27:04.206
They were girls together, as all know.

27:05.415 --> 27:08.168
Do you believe,
after what has since transpired,

27:08.252 --> 27:10.546
that there is some bond
between them still?

27:11.547 --> 27:12.548
Perhaps.

27:14.925 --> 27:16.093
Would that pain you?

27:18.053 --> 27:21.473
My concern is for the queen only.

27:21.557 --> 27:23.267
I'm no friend to the Hightowers.

27:23.350 --> 27:25.352
Well, there we are agreed,
though I believe Alicent

27:25.435 --> 27:27.271
is by nature a conspirator

27:27.354 --> 27:29.439
rather than one who openly deceives.

27:30.315 --> 27:32.484
Or perhaps a tool.

27:32.568 --> 27:34.236
Begging your pardon, my prince.

27:34.319 --> 27:37.823
It seems Vhagar has been sighted
leaving King's Landing...

27:38.866 --> 27:41.618
flying in the direction of the Riverlands.

27:42.202 --> 27:44.246
I would inform the queen, but...

27:44.329 --> 27:45.789
I will go.

28:01.597 --> 28:02.723
Your Grace!

28:03.932 --> 28:06.018
The atmosphere is fraught.

28:09.021 --> 28:12.524
I think it's best you do not
stray again from my charge.

28:13.275 --> 28:15.444
I would speak with the captain
of the household guard, Ser Soren.

28:15.527 --> 28:16.486
Where might he be?

28:16.570 --> 28:18.197
Any number of places.

28:19.615 --> 28:21.909
-I could have a message sent to him.
-Thank you, no.

28:21.992 --> 28:24.494
Please make sure that
the small council chamber is secure.

28:24.578 --> 28:26.455
-I will call a meeting there presently.
-Your Grace?

28:26.538 --> 28:27.915
I command it.

28:29.166 --> 28:30.876
At once, Ser Rickard.

28:30.959 --> 28:32.544
As you wish.

28:39.134 --> 28:41.094
He died fighting for his queen.

28:42.804 --> 28:44.389
As was his desire.

28:47.100 --> 28:48.602
He defied me.

28:51.188 --> 28:52.648
That is what sons do.

28:55.567 --> 28:57.194
There was another dragon.

28:58.695 --> 29:00.656
Sheepstealer, Baela says.

29:00.739 --> 29:02.032
A wild dragon?

29:03.200 --> 29:04.618
He had a rider.

29:06.578 --> 29:08.830
That's impossible.
A wild dragon cannot ever be tamed.

29:08.914 --> 29:12.542
They attacked Moondancer
and drew Jace to his death.

29:13.877 --> 29:15.671
How can the Greens have claimed another?

29:15.754 --> 29:17.881
-I want you to find them.
-It will be done.

29:24.763 --> 29:27.057
But there is first more pressing business.

29:27.140 --> 29:28.725
No, I have no stomach for it.

29:32.771 --> 29:34.606
Vhagar has left King's Landing.

29:52.958 --> 29:55.002
The boys who...

29:56.628 --> 29:58.088
clung to me, who...

30:00.173 --> 30:03.093
hid their little faces in my skirts, dead,

30:03.176 --> 30:06.596
so that I may sit upon a throne of swords?

30:12.477 --> 30:14.062
Will you let them die in vain?

30:42.341 --> 30:43.508
No, no.

31:12.037 --> 31:13.038
Well.

31:16.083 --> 31:17.459
I beg your pardon?

31:17.542 --> 31:20.462
What an industrious
little creature you are.

31:20.545 --> 31:22.631
Hither and thither. So much to do.

31:22.714 --> 31:24.674
You would do well
to remember yourself, Lord Jasper.

31:24.758 --> 31:27.094
I remember myself well enough.

31:27.928 --> 31:30.055
I remember you, too, Your Grace,

31:30.138 --> 31:33.809
snaking your way into the halls of power
when you were just a girl.

31:35.394 --> 31:36.603
So young.

31:38.438 --> 31:39.981
So bold.

31:42.651 --> 31:45.570
I served Viserys faithfully.
I served this realm faithfully.

31:45.654 --> 31:47.489
You did what you had to do.

31:48.865 --> 31:50.492
No man could deny you that.

31:54.121 --> 31:55.080
Life is short.

31:55.914 --> 31:56.998
The gods are cruel.

31:57.541 --> 32:02.045
We all find what enjoyment we can
as the world heads into darkness.

32:05.882 --> 32:07.300
You...

32:07.384 --> 32:08.343
for instance.

32:11.513 --> 32:14.391
You found much enjoyment.

32:17.310 --> 32:18.645
With Ser Criston.

32:20.355 --> 32:22.023
-Did you not?
-Lord--

32:22.899 --> 32:24.067
Lord Jasper.

32:24.151 --> 32:25.193
Much...

32:26.194 --> 32:27.404
pleasure.

32:27.487 --> 32:29.281
The penalty for this would be death.

32:29.364 --> 32:30.782
Then what is the penalty
for you running off

32:30.866 --> 32:32.242
to a secret meeting with the City Watch?

32:32.325 --> 32:34.119
What was your business there, I wonder?

32:34.202 --> 32:35.328
Lord Jasper, please.

32:36.496 --> 32:38.915
-Say that again.
-What?

32:40.250 --> 32:41.710
Plead with me.

32:43.211 --> 32:44.254
No!

32:57.601 --> 32:58.643
No!

32:58.727 --> 33:00.270
No! No!

33:01.229 --> 33:03.231
No! No!

33:04.608 --> 33:06.693
No! No!

33:06.776 --> 33:07.777
No!

33:11.281 --> 33:12.365
Lord Jasper.

33:17.746 --> 33:18.622
Orwyle...

33:19.456 --> 33:20.457
Good.

33:21.583 --> 33:23.418
Seems we have a traitor on our hands.

33:24.461 --> 33:26.004
I was just going to call for you,
Ser Soren.

33:26.087 --> 33:28.548
She'll need to be confined
where she can make no further trouble.

33:28.632 --> 33:30.175
Grand Maester, I beseech you.

33:30.258 --> 33:31.885
Ask her where she was an hour ago.

33:33.345 --> 33:35.472
I know not where she may have been.

33:36.223 --> 33:39.184
But I know what I have seen
here with my own eyes.

33:39.267 --> 33:40.268
Arrest him!

33:40.685 --> 33:43.230
He dares lay his hands
on the mother of the king!

33:43.313 --> 33:45.815
The queen dowager has betrayed us.

33:45.899 --> 33:48.151
Her own sworn protector has cautioned me.

33:48.235 --> 33:49.903
You will come with us, Lord Jasper.

33:49.986 --> 33:53.031
I am the Master of Laws,
for the sake of the gods.

33:54.074 --> 33:55.450
Unhand me!

34:03.625 --> 34:05.835
I'm in your debt, Grand Maester.

34:08.380 --> 34:10.715
I do not know what you have done,
Your Grace.

34:11.550 --> 34:13.467
I fear it is something desperate.

34:34.322 --> 34:36.116
Our deepest condolences, Your Grace.

34:37.492 --> 34:38.534
This...

34:38.618 --> 34:40.161
this tragic turn of events.

34:43.623 --> 34:45.667
I am going to King's Landing now.

34:46.458 --> 34:47.918
What? Your Grace, you cannot mean--

34:48.003 --> 34:49.879
I heard no ambiguity
in the queen's statement,

34:49.963 --> 34:51.840
Lord Bartimos, did you?

34:51.922 --> 34:53.842
I will fly with my lord husband

34:53.925 --> 34:55.635
and with my new riders as guards.

34:55.719 --> 34:58.555
That is all very well,
but you cannot enter the castle

34:58.638 --> 35:00.974
on your dragon, my queen.

35:01.057 --> 35:03.184
The Velaryon host is scattered.

35:03.268 --> 35:05.228
You will not have them to defend you.

35:05.312 --> 35:06.646
She has me.

35:06.730 --> 35:09.858
Aemond flies to Harrenhal
as Alicent promised.

35:09.941 --> 35:11.610
When he returns, our window will shut.

35:11.693 --> 35:16.573
Forgive me, my queen,
but this reeks of a snare.

35:16.656 --> 35:18.950
If it is, so be it. I'm done with talking.

35:22.370 --> 35:24.789
Let Ser Lorent choose how he will die.

35:31.630 --> 35:33.214
You will need this, I think.

35:38.219 --> 35:40.180
I hope you will send for me.

35:43.642 --> 35:45.935
Remember which one of us
has been faithful.

36:04.412 --> 36:07.123
Much has changed since I was away.

36:07.207 --> 36:08.583
You've taken a new advisor.

36:08.667 --> 36:11.336
She's done much for us.

36:11.419 --> 36:13.880
-For me.
-So I gather.

36:13.963 --> 36:16.174
I have no need of your approval.

36:17.092 --> 36:18.551
It was an observation.

36:21.763 --> 36:23.807
My prince. Your Grace.

36:27.602 --> 36:28.812
Syrax!

36:37.320 --> 36:39.614
Today, King's Landing receives its queen.

36:41.116 --> 36:43.243
You will fly cover.
Stay wide and keep watch.

36:43.326 --> 36:44.619
Let none approach from the sky.

36:44.703 --> 36:46.621
Is that simple enough for you?

36:47.956 --> 36:49.332
It is.

36:49.416 --> 36:51.126
Stay on guard until I send word.

36:51.209 --> 36:53.253
It will not at any point
be necessary for you

36:53.336 --> 36:54.754
to engage in thinking,

36:54.838 --> 36:58.383
or making decisions, or having ideas.

37:00.635 --> 37:03.304
-No, Your Grace.
-No.

37:05.098 --> 37:07.934
Once the city is taken,
we return our attention to Vhagar.

37:09.978 --> 37:12.647
From this moment,
all must proceed according to plan.

37:16.484 --> 37:18.069
Don't let me down.

37:51.686 --> 37:53.938
Helaena. Helaena.

37:55.607 --> 37:58.443
This is strange. It isn't the season.

37:58.526 --> 38:00.528
Rhaenyra Is coming.

38:00.612 --> 38:03.364
-I need you now.
-Will there be a battle?

38:03.448 --> 38:04.866
No. No.

38:04.949 --> 38:08.077
We will allow her to enter,
and then we will flee.

38:08.161 --> 38:09.954
You've spoken to her?

38:11.414 --> 38:12.665
But I've been delayed.

38:12.749 --> 38:14.584
It seems Ser Rickard has betrayed me.

38:15.668 --> 38:17.295
We must stand down
the sentries on the battlement

38:17.378 --> 38:18.880
and as many of the household guards
as we are able.

38:18.963 --> 38:20.006
They will think you mad.

38:21.132 --> 38:22.258
But they will heed a queen.

38:22.342 --> 38:24.511
You are a queen.

38:24.594 --> 38:26.221
Helena, you are the queen.

38:26.304 --> 38:27.764
Quickly.

38:28.848 --> 38:30.725
You said my father changed his mind.

38:31.684 --> 38:33.978
You made Aegon king, you and Ser Criston

38:34.062 --> 38:36.231
and my grandsire, and the septon.

38:36.314 --> 38:38.191
I made a mistake.

38:38.274 --> 38:40.235
-But you heard him.
-If I did or I didn't,

38:40.318 --> 38:41.611
I could no longer say.

38:41.694 --> 38:42.779
But Helaena...

38:44.030 --> 38:46.115
you told me not many days ago

38:46.199 --> 38:47.909
that you were happier
before you were queen.

38:48.785 --> 38:50.537
Words that pierced me like a spear.

38:52.247 --> 38:57.043
I think now not of what you may deserve,
but what might make you happy.

38:58.461 --> 39:00.463
You, I may yet redeem.

39:06.219 --> 39:09.222
I think I might like to keep chickens.

39:17.397 --> 39:19.190
-My queen.
-Your Grace.

39:21.943 --> 39:23.152
-Your Grace.
-My queen.

39:23.236 --> 39:24.529
You.

39:24.612 --> 39:26.781
-Who's your captain?
-Ser Freddryk, Your Grace.

39:32.036 --> 39:33.371
Is aught amiss, Your Grace?

39:33.454 --> 39:35.623
You are to stand down your station,
Ser Freddryk,

39:35.707 --> 39:37.542
at the command of the Queen Helaena.

39:39.502 --> 39:41.462
Standing orders, Your Grace.

39:41.546 --> 39:43.047
Any dragon but Vhagar, we strike.

39:43.131 --> 39:44.632
Your orders are rescinded.

39:45.216 --> 39:48.636
-But the prince regent--
-The prince regent has left the city.

39:48.720 --> 39:50.847
The queen is your authority now.

39:52.098 --> 39:54.267
I will not have any beast harmed.

39:58.146 --> 40:00.523
Rhaenyra Targaryen approaches,
Ser Freddryk.

40:01.691 --> 40:04.027
She comes with Prince Daemon
and more besides.

40:04.944 --> 40:06.195
The king has abdicated.

40:06.279 --> 40:08.573
The prince regent himself
has fled the city.

40:09.532 --> 40:11.326
Will you fight and be burned,

40:11.409 --> 40:13.036
and King's Landing along with you, or

40:13.119 --> 40:15.705
will you suffer her to enter,
and hope for peace?

40:15.788 --> 40:17.707
Her sons were always kind.

40:21.544 --> 40:22.670
Ser Freddryk.

40:58.206 --> 40:59.457
To Harrenhal.

41:00.416 --> 41:01.584
To Harrenhal!

41:44.627 --> 41:45.837
Dragon!

43:27.980 --> 43:29.941
I seek Daemon Targaryen.

43:31.359 --> 43:33.361
I confess, we had not been expecting you.

43:36.114 --> 43:37.406
Draw your sword.

43:39.033 --> 43:41.744
-Your Grace, I have no sword.
-Then get one!

43:45.456 --> 43:47.333
I do not wish to oppose you.

43:52.255 --> 43:54.715
I have not wielded a blade
these many years.

43:56.467 --> 44:00.263
Surely, there is some other way
you might find satisfaction?

44:00.847 --> 44:02.223
Hm?

44:05.726 --> 44:07.353
The army has decamped.

44:09.814 --> 44:11.816
There's nothing to stop you.

44:20.616 --> 44:21.701
Father!

45:35.233 --> 45:36.484
Help me.

45:41.197 --> 45:42.740
Help me...

48:02.797 --> 48:04.507
Alicent did as she promised.

48:06.509 --> 48:08.386
The true test is within.

48:11.680 --> 48:13.057
Do not be afraid.

48:15.684 --> 48:17.311
I've come to make things right.

48:47.633 --> 48:48.843
Wait.

49:20.416 --> 49:23.794
Who else dares rise
against us in our house?

50:04.877 --> 50:06.045
Your Grace.

50:37.701 --> 50:39.245
Halt!

50:47.169 --> 50:48.420
Where is Aegon?

50:48.504 --> 50:50.381
It is nothing to you.

50:50.464 --> 50:51.757
I have business with him.

50:51.840 --> 50:54.552
Is the upstart pup too craven
to face his queen?

50:54.635 --> 50:56.887
You are brazen, I credit you this.

50:57.930 --> 50:59.139
Brazen or thick.

51:01.225 --> 51:03.435
I suppose that depends
whether I win or lose.

51:07.314 --> 51:09.316
Now here's a thing I haven't seen before.

51:19.034 --> 51:20.578
Stay close, Rhaenyra.

51:40.723 --> 51:41.974
Well met...

51:42.725 --> 51:43.809
Ser Luthor.

51:46.020 --> 51:49.148
The City Watch remembers our commander,
Daemon Targaryen...

51:50.649 --> 51:52.568
and Queen Rhaenyra,

51:52.651 --> 51:54.820
the one true heir to the Iron Throne.

51:57.197 --> 51:59.617
The guards at the gates
have thrown down their swords.

51:59.700 --> 52:02.953
Do the same, or perish as traitors.

52:22.139 --> 52:25.017
The prince regent will not stand for this.

52:25.100 --> 52:27.311
-Nor will the Hand!
-Seize them!

52:29.813 --> 52:33.108
And with them all who wear
the Hightower sigil.

52:41.492 --> 52:43.494
You have my gratitude, Ser Luthor.

52:44.536 --> 52:47.956
It was Prince Daemon himself
who gave me this gold cloak...

52:49.291 --> 52:50.834
20 years ago.

52:51.710 --> 52:53.253
I knew I'd see you again one day.

52:55.005 --> 52:56.840
I wish I could say
I was so sure about you.

53:04.264 --> 53:05.974
It's your throne, my queen.

53:07.434 --> 53:08.811
Not yet.

53:10.854 --> 53:12.189
Bring Aegon...

53:13.357 --> 53:14.733
the Usurper...

53:15.859 --> 53:17.778
to me!

53:42.344 --> 53:44.096
-He is not here.
-Then where?

53:44.179 --> 53:45.431
I do not know.

53:47.015 --> 53:48.225
I swear it.

53:48.851 --> 53:49.852
He is fled,

53:49.935 --> 53:51.770
and the Master of Whisperers with him.

53:51.854 --> 53:53.021
How convenient.

53:53.105 --> 53:55.607
I remained here when Aegon
took the throne.

53:56.734 --> 53:58.569
I am no knight, I feared for my life.

53:59.653 --> 54:02.322
But I've done what I can,
as the queen dowager can attest.

54:02.406 --> 54:03.574
She's not here either.

54:06.368 --> 54:11.165
I pledge fealty to Viserys' rightful heir,

54:11.248 --> 54:13.500
queen by blood and by oath.

54:20.048 --> 54:23.719
If the Usurper has fled,
then we must take heads, as you well know,

54:23.802 --> 54:26.221
loath as I am to strike down a maester.

54:26.305 --> 54:27.973
You will kill me if you must.

54:30.184 --> 54:32.728
But I can offer you another
who might give you better...

54:33.896 --> 54:35.314
satisfaction.

54:50.496 --> 54:52.039
We cannot escape this way.

55:03.383 --> 55:05.469
-Release them.
-At once, my prince.

55:12.518 --> 55:14.853
-What has happened?
-Orwyle's offered you up.

55:15.979 --> 55:19.316
Delightful to witness you
turning on each other like spiders.

55:19.399 --> 55:22.903
This is her doing.
Conniving little bitch.

55:22.986 --> 55:25.864
Keep talking and I'll relieve you
of your cock before your head,

55:25.948 --> 55:27.157
just for the fun of it.

55:27.241 --> 55:28.909
If you would, my prince.

55:31.870 --> 55:34.623
A gift for you

55:34.706 --> 55:36.291
if you ever returned.

55:37.459 --> 55:39.336
From Lord Larys Strong.

56:35.434 --> 56:38.061
Lord Merryweather and Lady Fell,

56:38.145 --> 56:40.397
imprisoned for holding
to their oaths, Your Grace.

56:42.065 --> 56:45.027
-Ah, Lady Fell.
-My queen.

56:45.110 --> 56:47.195
Lord Merryweather. You have my gratitude.

56:49.364 --> 56:51.199
The Master of Laws,

56:51.283 --> 56:53.118
who plotted with the Usurper.

56:53.201 --> 56:55.454
You will hang for this!

56:55.537 --> 56:57.164
If you do not burn.

56:58.040 --> 56:59.708
Who of your council is left alive?

57:00.959 --> 57:04.838
The rats in the Black Cells
have grown uncommon big.

57:20.145 --> 57:22.481
No more than I expected.

57:38.455 --> 57:39.957
Kneel.

57:50.217 --> 57:52.761
I assume everyone else is dead.

57:56.515 --> 57:59.559
Aegon has fled, but our old friend
can stand in his place.

58:05.565 --> 58:07.734
Just get it over with, will you?

58:11.113 --> 58:12.406
They're watching.

58:23.875 --> 58:26.962
If you wish to rule,
show them you do not waver.

58:27.045 --> 58:28.839
I don't know if I can.

58:31.967 --> 58:33.301
Let Daemon do it.

58:37.347 --> 58:39.349
Spare me at least from being hacked at.

59:01.455 --> 59:03.707
If your father could see
what it's come to...

59:04.750 --> 59:06.376
he would never have imagined it.

59:06.460 --> 59:07.753
Speak no more!

59:14.718 --> 59:17.846
In this moment, you will become queen.

59:57.511 --> 59:58.762
I did my best--

01:00:23.703 --> 01:00:24.871
Tell my lady wife whatever--

01:02:05.096 --> 01:02:06.139
Clear!

01:02:08.391 --> 01:02:09.392
Clear!

01:02:10.352 --> 01:02:11.728
Stand aside!
